          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "<\/AT> Functional abdominal pain (FAP) according to the paediatric ROME III (pRIII) criteria appears to be highly prevalent among school children. The differentiation between organic and functional abdominal pain is a challenge. Indeed, the capacity of the pRIII criteria to identify patients with FAP is still debated."
